00:00.003 --> 00:00.004
♪ Florsheim monster

00:00.003 --> 00:00.004
♪ Running in

00:00.005 --> 00:00.006
♪ Usakotsu

00:00.005 --> 00:00.006
♪ Astro Fighter Sunred

00:00.007 --> 00:00.008
- - ♪Usakotsu will not throw it away here at the fear that someone might be watching.
- ♪Astro Fighter Sunred - ♪Short Corner

00:00.007 --> 00:00.008
- ♪Horror!
- ♪Operation Florsheim No. 1 - ♪To Mr. Astro Fighter Sunred

00:00.009 --> 00:00.010
♪On the way

00:00.009 --> 00:00.010
♪From Mister X

00:00.011 --> 00:00.012
♪Short Corner

00:00.013 --> 00:00.014
♪On the way

00:00.015 --> 00:00.016
♪End

00:00.480 --> 00:02.610
Gaima's Ambition

00:06.550 --> 00:08.170
Ah...

00:09.950 --> 00:11.870
I want a dog.

01:49.170 --> 01:51.470
Boy, am I thirsty.

01:53.160 --> 01:54.690
I better drink something.

01:56.170 --> 01:58.019
What should I get?

01:58.020 --> 02:00.660
Soda's probably best
for hot days like this.

02:02.320 --> 02:03.719
Oh, this one's new.

02:03.720 --> 02:05.220
I'll just get that then.

02:07.110 --> 02:09.930
Geez, I never have enough
change when I need it!

02:14.480 --> 02:15.939
Oh come on!

02:15.940 --> 02:18.620
I'm already dying of heat and thirst here!

02:23.050 --> 02:28.079
I guess machines nowadays
reject bills five times outta ten.

02:28.080 --> 02:29.819
That's higher than
Ichiro's batting average.

02:29.820 --> 02:32.019
It's quite disappointing
considering that we're in Japan.

02:32.020 --> 02:34.069
I mean things like Digital TV and
Blu-ray discs are pretty impressive,

02:34.070 --> 02:36.351
but we should really focus
on the bare necessities first.

02:38.860 --> 02:41.569
I usually can't finish a
350ml can by myself,

02:41.570 --> 02:43.390
but I guess it's not
much of a problem today.

02:47.780 --> 02:49.009
That was refreshing.

02:49.010 --> 02:50.320
Now, let's get going.

02:54.350 --> 02:55.350
Oh yeah!

02:55.400 --> 02:56.850
Where's that frying pan...

02:57.650 --> 02:59.190
I need to do something about this.

03:01.150 --> 03:04.830
What should I do, I can't get these
burnt noodle stains to come off!

03:07.030 --> 03:08.319
I guess I'll throw it away.

03:08.320 --> 03:10.750
I can just get another cheap one anyway.

03:11.540 --> 03:15.879
Oh no! They already collected
the metal trash for the week!

03:15.880 --> 03:17.039
What the hell,

03:17.040 --> 03:19.920
they usually tend to come
around in the afternoon.

03:21.150 --> 03:24.179
Then again it's kind of a hassle to go back
to the apartment just to put this away.

03:24.180 --> 03:27.420
Usakotsu won't throw it away here due to
the fear that someone might be watching.

03:27.570 --> 03:31.290
Oh well. I'll just have to throw it away
somewhere along the way to base.

03:33.770 --> 03:35.370
Screw it, I'll just throw it away here.

03:35.600 --> 03:38.699
I guess it's better off to throw it away
here with other metals than anywhere else.

03:38.700 --> 03:41.326
They probably won't even notice
when I put the lid back on anyway.

03:41.350 --> 03:42.760
Maybe it's a little big.

03:47.770 --> 03:49.210
S-Sunred!

03:49.910 --> 03:51.619
What are you hiding there?

03:51.620 --> 03:52.590
I'm not hiding anything.

03:52.620 --> 03:54.489
Aren't you one of Florsheim's monsters?

03:54.490 --> 03:55.490
Show me what you're hiding.

03:55.491 --> 03:57.189
It's none of your business!

03:57.190 --> 03:59.549
You're planning something
evil again, aren't you?

03:59.550 --> 04:01.269
Is that a bomb you got there?

04:01.270 --> 04:02.369
No, it's not!

04:02.370 --> 04:03.180
Show it to me!

04:03.181 --> 04:05.270
You annoying little...

04:05.770 --> 04:07.089
Die, Sunred!

04:07.090 --> 04:08.090
Demon Claw-

04:10.930 --> 04:12.849
I don't get you.

04:12.850 --> 04:15.919
What the hell were you doing
with a rusty old frying pan?

04:15.920 --> 04:17.310
Shut up.

04:21.420 --> 04:22.790
Oww...

04:26.290 --> 04:27.879
So, what's this?

04:27.880 --> 04:31.040
Why couldn't they just come
pick these things up twice a week?

04:34.320 --> 04:35.949
Moving on to the next story,

04:35.950 --> 04:40.169
the serial phantom killer
from Kawasaki is still at large,

04:40.170 --> 04:42.930
and reports show that
his victims are all female...

04:44.210 --> 04:45.210
Huh?

04:48.480 --> 04:51.429
It's quite unusual for you
to come pick me up like this.

04:51.430 --> 04:54.340
Don't be silly. I was just on my
way back from buying cigarettes.

05:02.830 --> 05:04.390
Hey!

05:04.730 --> 05:05.950
It's me, long time no see!

05:06.450 --> 05:08.220
By the way, are you going next month?

05:09.010 --> 05:11.649
Oh yeah, you haven't been
showing up all these years, huh.

05:11.650 --> 05:13.199
Feel free to drop by if
you change your mind!

05:13.200 --> 05:14.200
See ya!

05:18.180 --> 05:20.000
Who's he mistaking me for?

05:22.950 --> 05:23.560
Over here!

05:23.920 --> 05:24.960
Come on!

05:38.810 --> 05:39.879
What's this?

05:39.880 --> 05:42.959
I don't know anyone
who'd send me something.

05:42.960 --> 05:44.220
Maybe it's for Kayoko.

05:45.440 --> 05:46.930
What the, it's for <i>me</i>?

05:47.650 --> 05:49.910
Well it's got a name on it, for starters.

05:50.880 --> 05:54.229
Isn't this the back of a
Takajimaya wrapping paper?

05:54.230 --> 05:55.450
What could this possibly be?

05:58.480 --> 06:00.810
It's recorded over something else.

06:07.550 --> 06:08.749
Is it rolling?

06:08.750 --> 06:10.089
Yes it is.

06:10.090 --> 06:11.509
Doesn't this look weird?

06:11.510 --> 06:13.169
It looks good on you, Master Vamp.

06:13.170 --> 06:14.030
Really?

06:14.031 --> 06:15.099
Does it look like I'm
trying to hide something?

06:15.100 --> 06:16.579
Not at all. I'm going to roll the tape now.

06:16.580 --> 06:18.130
All right.

06:18.890 --> 06:19.560
Mwahaha.

06:19.760 --> 06:21.359
Greetings, Sunred.

06:21.360 --> 06:25.549
We are... yes, I will call
myself Mister X for now.

06:25.550 --> 06:28.480
Do you see this hostage, Sunred?

06:30.100 --> 06:30.970
Toshio...

06:31.010 --> 06:32.010
Toshio!

06:32.110 --> 06:32.720
Huh?

06:32.820 --> 06:34.020
Oh, umm...

06:34.200 --> 06:36.030
Waa! Save me!

06:36.230 --> 06:39.979
As you can see, he is just a little boy.

06:39.980 --> 06:44.230
How long will his little mind and
body will hold up in this situation?

06:44.231 --> 06:45.989
Hey! What are you doing?

06:45.990 --> 06:48.160
Let me go!

06:50.100 --> 06:52.399
Hey Geirus, stop the tape for a second.

06:52.400 --> 06:53.939
Come on now, you shouldn't do that.

06:53.940 --> 06:55.460
Usakotsu is not a toy.

06:55.640 --> 06:56.140
Let me go!

06:56.340 --> 06:58.490
Didn't you promise to be a good boy?

06:58.490 --> 07:00.159
Just bear with us for
a little longer, okay?

06:58.491 --> 07:06.491
Stop it! Stop!

07:00.160 --> 07:02.139
No! I want to play with the bunny!

07:02.140 --> 07:03.649
You're being so difficult.

07:03.650 --> 07:08.269
I'm really sorry, but could you babysit
Toshio for the time being Usakotsu?

07:08.270 --> 07:09.779
Screw that! Why do I have to do it?

07:09.780 --> 07:13.269
This is something only you can do.

07:13.270 --> 07:14.539
Really?

07:14.540 --> 07:15.540
I'm counting on you.

07:16.100 --> 07:17.410
All right then.

07:17.600 --> 07:18.600
Yay!

07:19.730 --> 07:22.120
All right. Roll the tape again, Geirus.

07:22.210 --> 07:22.660
Oh no!

07:22.661 --> 07:23.809
What's wrong?

07:23.810 --> 07:24.810
I'm so sorry!

07:25.010 --> 07:27.180
I forgot to press "pause."

07:27.780 --> 07:30.060
Do you think they might have found us out?

07:30.360 --> 07:31.680
Oh, I think we're good.

07:31.890 --> 07:33.479
Your back's been facing
the camera this whole time.

07:33.480 --> 07:34.949
I guess so.

07:34.950 --> 07:37.030
Okay, let's pick it up
from where we left off.

07:38.340 --> 07:39.559
Mwahaha.

07:39.560 --> 07:42.699
If you so desire to save this
unfortunate child, Sunred,

07:42.700 --> 07:45.469
come to the town square on
the first block tonight at seven!

07:45.470 --> 07:46.569
And cut!

07:46.570 --> 07:48.199
That's a wrap, you guys.

07:48.200 --> 07:49.749
Cut the tape, Geirus.

07:49.750 --> 07:50.819
Yes, sir.

07:50.820 --> 07:53.769
Master Vamp, where was the trash can again?

07:53.770 --> 07:55.046
It should be under the utensils shelf-

07:55.070 --> 07:56.390
Don't stop now!

08:00.910 --> 08:01.580
Take this!

08:01.581 --> 08:02.890
Hold up...

08:03.010 --> 08:05.479
I delivered the video tape, Master Vamp.

08:05.480 --> 08:07.139
I see, mwahaha.

08:07.140 --> 08:08.969
Hey, I'm thirsty.

08:08.970 --> 08:12.719
Thanks a lot for helping
us with the operation.

08:12.720 --> 08:16.020
You really saved our butts, Toshio.

08:16.400 --> 08:19.269
Can someone bring the
barley tea from the fridge?

08:19.270 --> 08:20.350
I got it!

08:20.750 --> 08:24.239
Oh yeah Master Vamp, what
should we do about Toshio's dinner?

08:24.240 --> 08:25.759
Huh, why?

08:25.760 --> 08:28.319
Oh, it's evening already, isn't it.

08:28.320 --> 08:30.080
What do you want for dinner, Toshio?

08:30.880 --> 08:33.159
We want to treat you to dinner.

08:33.160 --> 08:34.899
Then I want...

08:34.900 --> 08:35.790
Salisbury steak!

08:35.791 --> 08:37.169
Why don't we order
from the diner in front of-

08:37.170 --> 08:38.389
Oh that's fine.

08:38.390 --> 08:40.239
Salisbury steak isn't that hard to cook.

08:40.240 --> 08:42.309
We still have minced
meat in the freezer too.

08:42.310 --> 08:44.989
It costs like twelve to
thirteen bucks at the diner,

08:44.990 --> 08:46.909
while it costs nothing to cook at home.

08:46.910 --> 08:48.520
I have all the ingredients anyway.

08:50.730 --> 08:52.579
Huh? Wait a minute here.

08:52.580 --> 08:54.490
Are you serious, Toshio?

08:55.190 --> 08:56.459
Master Vamp!

08:56.460 --> 08:58.009
What's all the fuss about?

08:58.010 --> 09:00.569
Apparently, Toshio has
to go to turtoring today.

09:00.570 --> 09:02.479
Tutoring?

09:02.480 --> 09:03.529
Is it true?

09:03.530 --> 09:04.330
Y-Yeah.

09:04.331 --> 09:08.150
You should have told us earlier!

09:08.750 --> 09:09.700
Hello?

09:09.701 --> 09:13.469
Hi, My name is Vamp, and I'm part of
an evil organization called Florsheim...

09:13.470 --> 09:14.979
Ah yes, hello.

09:14.980 --> 09:17.099
Am I speaking to Toshio's mother?

09:17.100 --> 09:20.969
Actually we were taking
your son hostage today, and...

09:20.970 --> 09:22.339
Yes, that's right.

09:22.340 --> 09:23.999
We were taking him hostage.

09:24.000 --> 09:26.669
But Toshio just told us
he has tutoring today...

09:26.670 --> 09:28.889
Yes I'm very sorry.

09:28.890 --> 09:30.989
I really had no idea.

09:30.990 --> 09:33.669
We'll have one of our men
take him there right away.

09:33.670 --> 09:34.719
Yes.

09:34.720 --> 09:36.509
Yes, thank you for understanding.

09:36.510 --> 09:37.920
Have a nice day.

09:38.380 --> 09:43.359
It's six fifteen now, so if we hurry we
can make it to his seven o'clock tutoring.

09:43.360 --> 09:45.589
Sorry for the trouble, Toshio.

09:45.590 --> 09:49.169
I'm sorry. I just didn't
want to go to tutoring.

09:49.170 --> 09:51.299
That's okay.

09:51.300 --> 09:52.659
But what about the hostage thing?

09:52.660 --> 09:54.989
Don't worry about it.

09:54.990 --> 09:58.869
You can just help us out later
when you don't have tutoring, okay?

09:58.870 --> 10:00.919
We should get going, Master Vamp.

10:00.920 --> 10:02.410
Ah, hold on real quick.

10:03.360 --> 10:05.710
Take this with you, Toshio.

10:06.000 --> 10:08.619
Put the steak in between the
buns and make it a hamburger.

10:08.620 --> 10:10.569
The Salisbury steak is still warm,

10:10.570 --> 10:13.920
so if you put it in now the
buns are going to get all soggy.

10:14.450 --> 10:17.169
You shouldn't put the
bag on its side either,

10:17.170 --> 10:18.409
or else the sauce is going to seep through.

10:18.410 --> 10:19.120
Okay.

10:19.121 --> 10:20.390
Thanks, Master Vamp!

10:20.820 --> 10:24.519
It's dark so look out
for power lines, Geirus.

10:24.520 --> 10:25.969
Can I come over and play again?

10:25.970 --> 10:26.999
You betcha.

10:27.000 --> 10:28.409
Let's play the fighting game again.

10:28.410 --> 10:29.509
Fight! Fight!

10:29.510 --> 10:32.139
Don't come back!

10:32.140 --> 10:34.780
We'll get going then.

10:35.100 --> 10:36.679
Bye bye!

10:36.680 --> 10:39.080
Bye bye!

11:03.810 --> 11:06.859
I wonder if Toshio's had
his Salisbury steak already.

11:06.860 --> 11:09.480
You've got some ketchup
on your mouth, Master Vamp.

11:10.380 --> 11:11.430
He does!

11:19.940 --> 11:21.079
Those punk bitches.

11:21.080 --> 11:23.719
I'm going to beat them up real good!

11:23.720 --> 11:25.339
Astro Fighter Sunred:

11:25.340 --> 11:27.429
This is a story about the
conflict between good and evil

11:27.430 --> 11:29.850
which takes place in the city of Kawasaki.
